C2. LINE-BY-LINE READ OF ALL THREE PUBLISH PATHS — MET.
  Read in full: storage.go:543-580 (createExclusive), storage.go:621-660 (atomicWrite),
  auth.go:99-146 (saveConfig). All three have the identical sequence
  Write -> fileSync -> Close -> Chmod -> Rename/Link -> syncDir.
  fileSync error handling, all three sites: `if err := fileSync(f); err != nil {
  _ = f.Close(); return <err> }` at storage.go:563, storage.go:644, auth.go:129 —
  identical shape to the Write-failure branch directly above it, so the publish
  aborts, the existing `defer func() { _ = os.Remove(tmpPath) }()` cleans staging,
  destination untouched.
  syncDir error handling, all three sites: storage.go:580 `return syncDir(dir)`,
  storage.go:660 `return syncDir(dir)`, auth.go:145 `return syncDir(baseDir)`, each
  preceded by `if err := os.Rename/os.Link(...); err != nil { return err }`. No site
  discards either seam's error; there is no `_ =` on either seam anywhere in
  non-test code (verified by grep of all 11 fileSync/syncDir occurrences module-wide).
  saveConfig wrapping style: the fileSync error is wrapped `fmt.Errorf("failed to
  write config: %w", err)`, matching its adjacent Write/Close/Chmod branches; the
  syncDir error is returned unwrapped, which matches the unwrapped `os.Rename` error
  return immediately above it (and the pre-change `return os.Rename(...)`). Internally
  consistent and errors.Is-transparent — TestSaveConfigDirSyncFailurePropagates
  asserts via errors.Is and passes.
  syncDir syncs the DIRECTORY, not the file — storage.go:524-533:
      var syncDir = func(dir string) error {
          d, err := os.Open(dir)        // opens the dir path, not the staging file
          if err != nil { return err }  // open error wins, returns immediately
          err = d.Sync()
          if cerr := d.Close(); err == nil { err = cerr }  // sync error beats close error
          return err
      }
  First error among open/sync/close wins, as specified.
  Completeness: `grep 'os.Rename\|os.Link' internal/services/storage/*.go` (non-test)
  returns exactly 3 hits — storage.go:574, storage.go:657, auth.go:142 — i.e. the three
  paths fixed are ALL the publish paths in the package; none was missed.

